.env
data/
output/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Live profile tree (assets/ + prompts/) and workspaces: machine-local state,
# loaded from the tracked bundles in profiles/. A fresh clone packs nothing —
# `tools/profile.sh unpack <name>` materializes the live tree and writes the
# .bm/profile pointer that bm-core::profile::verify gates runners on.
/assets/
/prompts/
/workspaces/

# Inductor state, run logs
.bm/
*.log
.venv/

# Working documents: audits, proposals, plans, notes. They describe a moment in
# the code's life rather than the code itself, and are regenerated on demand —
# so they live in one ignored directory instead of being pattern-matched by
# name, which would risk catching a document that should be tracked. None of
# them is a build input.
/.docs/

# Personal voice data. `voices.default.json` (the shipped catalogue) IS tracked;
# these three are the machine-local half — the clones enrolled on this machine,
# the sample pool tagged from their filenames, and the reference clips both are
# built from. A fresh clone simply has no clones, which is a valid state
# (see `enrolled_voices` / `ensure_voices`).
/voices.json
/voice-pool.json
/refs/

# Worker display name, drawn once at startup and kept (`bm-agent`).
# Machine-local like voices.json: two boxes may honestly draw the same name.
/worker.alias

# OS noise
.DS_Store

# Rust build output
rust/target/
**/target/

# The sea-g2p phoneme dictionary: 60 MB, and byte-identical to upstream at the
# pinned commit (hash in rust/vendor/sea-g2p/VENDORED.md). It is a runtime
# artifact the bake step fetches, not source — committing it would put 60 MB of
# binary in every clone for a file that is verifiable by hash instead.
/rust/vendor/sea-g2p/python/
/models/

